      "writtenOn": "2019-02-15T23:46:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I revert it to have simply \u0027-m\u0027.\n\nNow I understand matthewb@\u0027s comment on specifying explicitly boolean type: If the default value should be changed in future, then the existence of parameter also should be translated into a different meaning.\n\nHowever, we already have the mixed style among boolean parameters in iteflash.\n\u0027--debug\u0027 simply enables the debug mode, and is not likely to have the default value changed in future. Likewise \u0027--i2c_mux\u0027 would simply enable i2c_mux, and the default value should not be changed, I believe.",
